    "summary_one_sentence": "In the high-stakes aftermath of a covert mission, undercover Indian operative Hamza navigates the deadly street wars of Lyari to dismantle a transnational terror network while waging a bloody personal war against the ruthless Major Iqbal.",
    "summary_short": "Following the collapse of gang hierarchies in Karachi's Lyari district, undercover Indian agent Hamza consolidates power within the local syndicate to target the masterminds behind devastating terror attacks. As corrupt officials, rival factions, and law enforcement close in, Hamza finds his covert assignment spiraling into a deadly personal conflict. Facing the formidable ISI officer Major Iqbal, he is forced to risk everything to dismantle the criminal enterprise operating across borders. Ultimately, his patriotic duty blurs into a violent quest for retribution where survival demands becoming as dangerous as the enemies he hunts.",
    "summary_long": "After eliminating key gang leaders in Karachi, undercover Indian intelligence officer Jaskirat Singh Rangi, operating as Hamza, tightens his grip on Lyari's criminal underworld. Hamza maneuvers through a complex web of syndicates, corrupt politicians, and rogue military handlers to expose the architects of terror operations directed against India. His primary target becomes Major Iqbal, a calculating ISI officer controlling counterfeit currency networks, weapons shipments, and militant cells. As rival gangsters challenge his control and police forces launch aggressive crackdowns, Hamza struggles to preserve his cover and safeguard those close to him. The stakes heighten when unexpected internal betrayals and shifting alliances expose his network to constant threat. Forced to take extreme measures to prevent operational failure, Hamza engages in psychological warfare and lethal ambushes against competing factions. Major Iqbal eventually uncovers Hamza's true identity, escalating their cat-and-mouse game into an aggressive direct confrontation. In a violent showdown across the streets and shipping docks of Lyari, Hamza endures heavy physical and moral strain to neutralize Iqbal's operations, ultimately proving how thin the boundary between patriot and monster becomes in total war.",
    "synopsis": "Dhurandhar: The Revenge is an intense action thriller set within the volatile underworld of Karachi's Lyari neighborhood. Deep undercover as a local syndicate figure, Indian intelligence agent Hamza balances a double life among brutal gangsters, corrupt political leaders, and intelligence handlers. When his assignment to dismantle a vast terror financing and smuggling network becomes deeply personal, Hamza must navigate deadly power struggles while keeping his primary target in sight: Major Iqbal, a ruthless military officer driving terror operations from the shadows. Blending geopolitical intrigue, gritty street combat, and dramatic stakes, the story explores the immense sacrifices and moral cost of an agent driven to defend his country at all costs.",
